#. TRANSLATORS: ${BTN_CHECK_ANOTHER_FILE} and ${BTN_TRUST_THIS_KEY}
#. will be replaced with the translated "Check Another File"/
#. "Trust this key" button labels - keep both placeholders,
#. including the braces, exactly as-is. The straight quotes
#. around each are just English's own convention - please use
#. your language's own quotation marks instead (e.g. « », „",
#. etc.) if that reads more naturally.
#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:908
#, sh-format
msgid "This only shows as FAILED because you didn't trust this signing key - the cryptographic check itself already came back GOOD (see the technical details below). If you're confident this is the genuine key (e.g. you've checked its fingerprint against the distro's own official site or keyserver listing), click \"${BTN_CHECK_ANOTHER_FILE}\" and choose \"${BTN_TRUST_THIS_KEY}\" this time."
msgstr ""

#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:910
msgid "The cryptographic check itself already came back GOOD (see the technical details below) - this only shows as FAILED because the key couldn't be saved for future trust (see the technical details for why). Feel free to try again."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: ${BTN_CHECK_ANOTHER_FILE} will be replaced with
#. the translated "Check Another File" button label - keep the
#. placeholder, including the braces, exactly as-is. The
#. straight quotes around it are just English's own convention
#. - please use your language's own quotation marks instead
#. (e.g. « », „", etc.) if that reads more naturally.
#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:918
#, sh-format
msgid "You pointed this tool at a checksum-listing file, not a single ISO - it can cover many ISOs at once, so there's no one file to check unless exactly one of the ones it mentions is actually present here (see the technical details below for which). Use \"${BTN_CHECK_ANOTHER_FILE}\" and point at the actual .iso file instead."
msgstr ""

#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:920
msgid "The checksum file that lists this ISO's hash failed its own verification (bad/untrusted signature, or its key couldn't be confirmed) - nothing in it can be trusted. Re-download the checksum/signature files (and probably the ISO too), ideally from a different mirror."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: ${CHECKSUM_INFO_SAFE} will be replaced with the
#. checksum-listing file's name (e.g. "SHA256SUMS") - keep the
#. placeholder, including the braces, exactly as-is.
#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:926
#, sh-format
msgid "This ISO was checked against a signed checksum listing (${CHECKSUM_INFO_SAFE}) that IS validly signed - but the ISO's own hash doesn't match what's listed. The checksum list itself is trustworthy; this particular download is not. Re-download the ISO, ideally from a different mirror."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: ${BTN_CHECK_ANOTHER_FILE} will be replaced with
#. the translated "Check Another File" button label - keep the
#. placeholder, including the braces, exactly as-is. The
#. straight quotes around it are just English's own convention
#. - please use your language's own quotation marks instead
#. (e.g. « », „", etc.) if that reads more naturally.
#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:934
#, sh-format
msgid "No direct signature file was found for this ISO, and none of the checksum-listing files found nearby mention this exact ISO filename either. If this distro uses a different naming convention, use \"${BTN_CHECK_ANOTHER_FILE}\" and point at the right file directly."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: ${BTN_CHECK_ANOTHER_FILE} will be replaced with
#. the translated "Check Another File" button label - keep the
#. placeholder, including the braces, exactly as-is. The
#. straight quotes around it are just English's own convention
#. - please use your language's own quotation marks instead
#. (e.g. « », „", etc.) if that reads more naturally.
#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:942
#, sh-format
msgid "The file names don't match, so this signature file may simply not belong to this .iso. Use \"${BTN_CHECK_ANOTHER_FILE}\" and pick the signature file named exactly like the ISO plus .sig/.asc/.gpg."
msgstr ""

#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:944
msgid "On top of the signature not matching, this signing key also isn't one of the officially documented MX/antiX keys - treat this file as untrustworthy and re-download from an official source."
msgstr ""

#: verify-iso-sig-gui.sh:946
msgid "The ISO may be corrupted, or the download was incomplete or tampered with - try re-downloading it, ideally from a different mirror."
msgstr ""

